BLINK PTHREAD BUILD 3rd obstacle (sandcastle/portabox): self-shim fixed module-eval, but threaded build now fails smoke with TypeError Module.wasmExports undefined in blink-core.js writeStr. Cause: with -pthread, emscripten initializes wasmExports asynchronously after the pthread worker pool spins up; blink-core.js accesses wasmExports synchronously right after callMain. Fix: await Module.ready / runtime-initialized before touching wasmExports in the threaded path. Sequence of pthread obstacles: (1) configure probe cant run wasm->fork/threads detect no [unfixable for fork; HAVE_THREADS is define-gated not probe-gated so threads ARE on], (2) self undefined at module eval [fixed: globalThis.self shim], (3) wasmExports async-init race [pending]. ALSO confirmed: emscripten has NO fork() at all, so pipes/concurrent-processes via fork are impossible regardless; concurrent GUI+CLI must use cooperative scheduling or pthreads, not fork. Single-threaded build (sha 80e9953392) is the working baseline live in webix main.